# CFO Briefing — H1 2026 Close (prepared 2026-11 board pack run-up)

Source: `finance/ledger.csv` (87 entries, all 2026 H1, every account mapped via `finance/chart_of_accounts.csv`). Figures in R$.

## Monthly P&L

| Month | Revenue | Gross margin % | EBITDA |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2026-01 | 200,510.87 | 69.60 | -58,400.21 |
| 2026-02 | 237,447.61 | 66.27 | -77,444.95 |
| 2026-03 | 226,248.16 | 62.52 | -110,572.63 |
| 2026-04 | 238,163.26 | 66.15 | -109,555.49 |
| 2026-05 | 261,267.29 | 67.17 | -94,257.63 |
| 2026-06 | 272,391.57 | 62.48 | -443,892.55 |

H1 revenue: 1,436,028.76 · H1 EBITDA: -894,123.46

## Month narrative
- Jan–May: steady top-line growth (+30% Jan→May), gross margin stable in the 62–70% band, EBITDA burn between -58k and -110k/mo. May was the best burn month of Q2.
- June: revenue hit an H1 high (272.4k) but EBITDA collapsed to -443.9k, driven by sales (paid media 62.4k + sales team 89.5k = 151.9k, the heaviest S&M month) and two full engineering payroll lines (84.6k + 91.0k = 175.5k, second-highest R&D month). Gross margin also dipped to 62.5% (cloud/GPU 55.9k).
- Refunds: account 3.1.09 carries two "Refund customer Kestrel" charges, 6,814.15 in March and 8,634.37 in May, already netted out of revenue.

## Burn & runway (board's definition, per finance/README.md)
- Burn = average monthly negative EBITDA of the last three closed months (Apr, May, Jun): (109,555.49 + 94,257.63 + 443,892.55) / 3 = **352,568.56 / month**.
- Cash at latest close (30/06/2026, cash_balance.txt): **R$ 1,847,350.40** (down 461,837.60 from 2,309,188.00 at 31/05/2026).
- Runway = 1,847,350.40 / 352,568.56 = **5.20 months** → cash-out around **late November / early December 2026** if June's cost base persists.

## Presentation caveats
- The June blowout is a one-month weight in the 3-month burn average; if Apr–May cost levels return (~100k/mo burn), runway stretches past 12 months. Present both: the board formula's 5.2 months, and the underlying trend.
- Cash fell 461.8k in June vs June EBITDA of -443.9k plus +5.6k net financial income; the ~23.6k gap is timing/non-P&L cash movement not visible in this ledger.
- Assumptions: EBITDA = revenue − COGS − (S&M + R&D + G&A); financial accounts (6.1.x) excluded from EBITDA but included in cash reality; "closed months" = Apr–Jun 2026.


